.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt ASYSFS 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm asysfs
.Nd system file system in the layout of Android
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the file system as a module at boot time, place the following
line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
asysfs_load="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
To mount it in a jail, add a line such as the following to
.Xr jail.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mount += "asysfs $path/sys asysfs ro 0 0";
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file system gives a
.Pa /sys
tree with the names and the text layout that Android programs read
on Linux.
It is intended for a jail that runs Android programs on the native
.Fx
ABI, together with
.Xr aprocfs 4 .
It does not use the
.Xr linux 4
ABI.
A program sees
.Nm
only where it is mounted.
.Pp
The file system contains:
.Bl -tag -width "devices/system/cpu/possible"
.It Pa devices/system/cpu/online
The CPUs that run threads, in the list format of
.Xr cpuset 1 ,
for example
.Ql 0-3 ,
and a newline.
The number of CPUs in the list is the
.Va hw.ncpu
value.
.It Pa devices/system/cpu/present
The same list as
.Pa online :
.Fx
has no CPU hot plug.
.It Pa devices/system/cpu/possible
The range from 0 to the
.Va kern.smp.maxid
value, and a newline.
.El
.Pp
All files are read-only.
.Nm
is a
.Xr pseudofs 9
file system.
.Sh EXAMPLES
To mount an
.Nm
file system on
.Pa /compat/android/sys :
.Pp
.Dl "mount -t asysfs asysfs /compat/android/sys"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cpuset 1 ,
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr aprocfs 4 ,
.Xr jail.conf 5 ,
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr pseudofs 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
file system first appeared in the freebsd-android-native fork of
.Fx 15.1 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Ayeed Shaikh Aq Mt Ayeed.AI10@race.reva.edu.in
.Sh BUGS
.Xr fsync 2
on an
.Nm
node returns 0, as on every
.Xr pseudofs 9
file system.
